From 666b179b651e0d154b1bdaaaee9449e57f963c08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Murphy <mike@sugarmillgang.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 04:31:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net/atlantic: fix delayed MACsec alarm use-after-free on stop

atl_dev_link_update() unconditionally schedules a 1-second
rte_eal_alarm_set() callback (atl_dev_delayed_handler(), which
calls atl_dev_configure_macsec()) on every link status transition,
regardless of whether MACsec is even enabled - the handler itself
returns immediately if it isn't. Neither atl_dev_stop() nor
atl_dev_close() ever cancelled this pending alarm.

If the port is stopped/closed within that 1-second window - readily
hit under rapid application restart / interface-cycling, since any
link-up transition arms the timer - the alarm fires afterward on
DPDK's interrupt thread and dereferences a dev/dev_private pointer
that rte_eth_dev_close() may already have freed. Observed as a
SIGSEGV inside atl_dev_configure_macsec(), called from
eal_alarm_callback(), against a null dev_private pointer, consistently
reproducible by racing a second process's start against a first
process's rapid stop/close on the same port.

Cancel the pending alarm at the top of atl_dev_stop(), so it can
never outlive the device it was scheduled against.

Fixes: 9f7e206a4cfd ("net/atlantic: configure MACsec from interrupt handler")

Signed-off-by: Mike Murphy <mike@sugarmillgang.com>
---
 drivers/net/atlantic/atl_ethdev.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/atlantic/atl_ethdev.c b/drivers/net/atlantic/atl_ethdev.c
index 2925dc2478..3d6a510db0 100644
--- a/drivers/net/atlantic/atl_ethdev.c
+++ b/drivers/net/atlantic/atl_ethdev.c
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ static int eth_atl_dev_init(struct rte_eth_dev *eth_dev);
 static int  atl_dev_configure(struct rte_eth_dev *dev);
 static int  atl_dev_start(struct rte_eth_dev *dev);
 static int atl_dev_stop(struct rte_eth_dev *dev);
+static void atl_dev_delayed_handler(void *param);
 static int  atl_dev_set_link_up(struct rte_eth_dev *dev);
 static int  atl_dev_set_link_down(struct rte_eth_dev *dev);
 static int  atl_dev_close(struct rte_eth_dev *dev);
@@ -612,6 +613,15 @@ atl_dev_stop(struct rte_eth_dev *dev)
 	PMD_INIT_FUNC_TRACE();
 	dev->data->dev_started = 0;
 
+	/* atl_dev_link_update() schedules this alarm on every link status
+	 * change with a 1s delay, unconditionally (regardless of whether
+	 * MACsec is even in use - atl_dev_configure_macsec() just no-ops
+	 * early if it's not). If the port is stopped/closed before that
+	 * alarm fires, it runs against a dev/dev_private that may already
+	 * be freed. Cancel it here so a pending alarm can never outlive the
+	 * device it was scheduled against. */
+	rte_eal_alarm_cancel(atl_dev_delayed_handler, (void *)dev);
+
 	/* disable interrupts */
 	atl_disable_intr(hw);
 
-- 
